      "side": 1,
      "message": "The scope of this change is simply to check sink\u0027s PACS before creating broadcast streams, and it\u0027s not intended to resolve other dynamic audio codec configs cases, e.g. remote updates PACS while broadcast. So if the config is not available we will just proceed with whatever preferred by the application side.\n\nAnd as I understand, the selectable codec configs will be provided by sinks upon device connections. Then when we started the broadcast with those connected devices, we will check the previously saved configs. \nIs your concern that the configs are not updated before we started the broadcast? I didn\u0027t understand why this is related to the handover cases.",
